course: dictionary
lesson: 8132
title: Replacement and its meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A replacement is something new that takes the place of something broken, lost or gone. «Titanium is also used for hip replacements because the body accepts it well.» Here the replacements are new hip parts that take the place of damaged ones.
explain: Replacement can also mean the act of putting something new in place of something old. Read the words around it. If the sentence is about a new thing, the word means the thing. If the sentence is about swapping, the word means the act of swapping.
explain: «Losing something has a cost; earning a replacement by chores or saving teaches you to look after things.» Here a replacement is the new item you get after losing the old one. Test your meaning by swapping in "new item" and checking that the sentence still makes sense.
explain: «If something is faulty, meaning broken when it should not be, the law usually gives you a refund, a repair or a replacement.» Here a replacement is one of three choices when something does not work. The clues are faulty and refund, so you know it is about goods going wrong.
fact: A replacement is a new thing or person that takes the place of one that is broken, lost or gone.
fact: Replacement can also mean the act of putting something new in place of something old.
fact: «A replacement for» means something that stands in for something else, as in «a replacement for a broken toy».
fact: «With replacement» is a maths phrase: you put an item back before you pick again.
fact: «Faulty» means broken or not working when it should be, so a faulty item may get a refund, a repair or a replacement.
exercise: «Titanium is also used for hip replacements because the body accepts it well.» What are hip replacements? | Hips that have been painted | *New hip parts that take the place of damaged ones | A kind of dance move | Old metal from a scrap yard
exercise: «Losing something has a cost; earning a replacement by chores or saving teaches you to look after things.» What does this sentence teach? | Saving is only for grown-ups | Losing things is always fun | *Looking after things, because losing them costs you | Chores are never useful
exercise: In maths, what does «with replacement» mean? | *You put the item back before picking again | You break the item first | You hide the item under the table | You never pick the item again
test: «If something is faulty, meaning broken when it should not be, the law usually gives you a refund, a repair or a replacement.» In this sentence, what is a replacement? | A refund of your money | A bag to carry the item in | *A new item given in place of the faulty one | A repair done to the old item
test: In the phrase «a replacement for the broken toy», what does «for» show? | The toy was made of wood | The toy is a present for someone | *The new toy is taking the place of the broken one | The toy was broken on purpose
exam: The replacement of the old roof took a whole week. What does replacement mean here? | A roof that is too big for the house | The act of putting a new roof in place of the old one | *The act of putting a new roof in place of the old one, so the old one is gone | A roof painted in bright colours
